---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/astro/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/astro/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · YOMXXX"
  description="About YOMXXX — a personal engineering log on the AI frontier, written by an applied AI engineer. Three essays a week, Monday / Wednesday / Friday."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <span>yomxxx</span> / <span class="cur">about</span>
    </div>
    <h1><span class="prefix">▸</span>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">Who I am · why this blog · how to reach me.</p>

    <div class="avatar-row">
      <img src="/avatar.jpeg" alt="YOMXXX" class="avatar" width="120" height="120" />
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        I'm an applied AI engineer working on LLM-driven systems — agents, RAG, and the
        production infrastructure that holds them up. Day to day that means reading papers,
        reading other people's code, and shipping systems that have to stay up. This blog is
        where that work gets written down.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this blog</h2>
      <p>
        I read and build a lot, and I'd rather externalize my notes than let them rot in a
        markdown drawer. Every essay here starts from something I actually needed to understand —
        a paper I had to evaluate, a tool I had to run, an architecture decision I had to defend.
      </p>
      <p>
        A note on cadence: this blog started in May 2026 and ran at five posts a day for a
        while. That was a mistake — volume crowded out depth, and it read like what it was.
        Since October 2026 the schedule is <strong>three essays a week (Monday, Wednesday,
        Friday)</strong>, and each one has to be something I'd still want to reference six
        months later.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>workshop</strong> · production lessons, code-first — code I actually ran, with the real output</li>
        <li><strong>long-form</strong> · architecture &amp; systems, with an argument rather than a summary</li>
        <li><strong>paper</strong> · arXiv distilled with engineering bias — can I use this, and where does it break</li>
        <li><strong>tools</strong> · honest reviews with hands-on comparison data</li>
        <li><strong>weekly</strong> · the AI week in 5 bullets (archive, paused for now)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Original work</h2>
      <p>
        The code behind most workshop posts lives on
        <a href="https://github.com/YOMXXX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my GitHub</a>.
        If a post claims a number, it came from a run I did — not from a README.
      </p>

      <h2>Site history</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>May 2026</strong> — first post; static Astro site on Cloudflare Pages</li>
        <li><strong>2026</strong> — 500+ essays across workshop, paper, long-form, tools, weekly</li>
        <li><strong>October 2026</strong> — switched from daily volume to three curated essays a week</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>EEAT note</h2>
      <p>
        Every article carries author and timestamps. Code I publish has been run; opinions I
        publish I've held for at least a week before writing them down. If I got something
        wrong, the contact page reaches me directly and I correct posts in place.
      </p>

      <h2>How to reach me</h2>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/contact">contact</a> page, or open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/YOMXXX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 24px 40px; }
  .breadcrumb { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--color-text-faint); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .breadcrumb span { color: var(--color-accent-green); }
  .breadcrumb .cur { color: var(--color-accent-amber); }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 26px;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  h1 .prefix { color: var(--color-accent-green); margin-right: 6px; }
  .avatar-row {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .avatar {
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .lead {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
</style>
